// @run
// @log 1
// @log 7
// @hint redundant type annotation: `a` is inferred as `{r: i32}[]` — remove it to lean on inference
// THE MODULE-SCOPE TWIN OF THE READ-ONLY COVARIANT BINDING (D822).
//
// This is `list-covariant-readonly-pass.vl`'s first half with the enclosing `function f()`
// removed, and until this fixture it was `vl check` rc 0 and an INVALID MODULE while the
// function-scope original ran. D791 hooked the widening at the seven delivery forms
// `letRefListDestSlot` enumerates, and a module GLOBAL is not one of them: it is not a
// `let`, its cell is `globalRefListSlot`, and its initializer is emitted by the synthetic
// START FUNCTION rather than by `emitLetDeclStmt`.
//
// A CONST global's init is a wasm CONSTEXPR and cannot carry a copy loop — but a global
// whose init reads another global is non-constexpr by construction (`globalIsNonConst`), so
// it always runs in the start function, which is a real function with a real frame. That is
// the eighth delivery form and the only place it could go.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
const a: Circle[] = [{ r: 7 }]
const b: Shape[] = a
print(b.length)
print(a[0].r)
